// EXPECT: FAIL
// A doubled colon where the supertype path belongs ("foo::") is not valid
// syntax, so this file must not parse.
//
// Confirmed: the parser reports "block looking for closing }" at line 2 and
// consumes 0 of 56 bytes, and adlmem exits 1 on that byte-count mismatch.
// Note what catches it is the mismatch, not the parser's own return value -
// parse() still returns true and prints "Success" (see cpp/ToDo's Standing
// note on errors not propagating). The abandoned attempt does leave a
// partial side effect in the store: a bare `foo : Object` with no supertype
// and none of its children, visible if you run this with -a.
TOP {
	foo:: {
		bar {
		}
	}

	foo {
		bat: {
		}
	}
}
